    "recorded": [
      {
        "key": "non_authoritative_from_core",
        "statement": "Core's own item-list, item-detail and health payloads carry `non_authoritative: true`; the inspector reads that field rather than asserting it. Source: memory/api.py."
      },
      {
        "key": "no_retain_endpoint",
        "statement": "There is no public retain endpoint: content reaches the engine only through a worker acting on a job derived from committed truth. Source: memory/api.py docstring."
      },
      {
        "key": "no_bank_selector",
        "statement": "There is no public bank selector: the bank is derived from the item's own scope, so an agent cannot choose `jasmine-global` or promote project content into it. Source: memory/api.py docstring."
      },
      {
        "key": "reflect_is_human_only",
        "statement": "`reflect` requires `memory:reflect`, which key issuance will not grant to an agent; it is the only path that runs the engine's generator and is unreachable from a Context build. It is out of this slice. Source: memory/api.py docstring."
      },
      {
        "key": "authorisation_from_actor",
        "statement": "Project authorisation is decided from the authenticated actor, never from a body field or a query parameter; an unauthorised project is reported as `not_found` so the inspector cannot enumerate another project's work. Source: memory/api.py docstring."
      },
      {
        "key": "empty_not_everything",
        "statement": "An actor with no grants gets an empty list rather than the whole database. Source: memory/api.py `list_jobs`/`list_items`/`list_traces`."
      },
      {
        "key": "agent_redaction",
        "statement": "An agent key may read jobs but only for a project it may read, and engine-derived text is withheld because error summaries can carry it. Source: memory/api.py `list_jobs`."
      },
      {
        "key": "memory_is_not_authority",
        "statement": "Memory is NON_AUTHORITATIVE: it cannot change Rule or State, and no view may present it as Truth. Sources: taskbook §6 and memory/api.py."
      },
      {
        "key": "credentials_stay_in_core",
        "statement": "Engine credentials never reach the browser; the engine lives behind Core. Sources: taskbook §6 and memory/transport.py."
      },
      {
        "key": "health_probe_not_in_a_request",
        "statement": "`health.report(probe=True)` can add a `probe` key, but probe is reachable only from the CLI and the worker, never from a request handler, so a request response carries the 17 report keys plus `non_authoritative`. Source: memory/health.py, memory/api.py."
      },
      {
